Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Mouse settings for a guest driven from a browser, so one PS/2 count is one guest pixel with no pointer acceleration: the page can then
; predict the guest pointer's position exactly and set the pointer speed in one place. ReactOS 0.4.16 ships with MouseSpeed 1 and thresholds
; 6 and 10 but did not accelerate in v86 when measured; these values make that explicit. SmoothMouseXCurve and SmoothMouseYCurve are not
; set: ReactOS's win32k does not read them.
;
; (c) Copyright 2026 Liminal HQ, Scott Morris
; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Control Panel\Mouse]
"MouseSpeed"="0"
"MouseThreshold1"="0"
"MouseThreshold2"="0"
"MouseSensitivity"="10"
